    "If f(x) = -2x + 9, what is f(-5)?::19|20|18|-19": "Plug negative 5 in for x: negative 2 times negative 5, plus 9, which is 10, plus 9, giving 19.",
    "If f(x) = -9x - 30, what is f(-9)?::51|50|52|-51": "Plug negative 9 in for x: negative 9 times negative 9, minus 30, which is 81, minus 30, giving 51.",
    "A line passes through (-7, -6) and (8, -21). What is its slope?::0|-2|1|-1": "Slope is the change in y over the change in x: negative 21 minus negative 6, over 8 minus negative 7, which is negative 15 over 15, giving negative 1.",
    "A line passes through (-1, 19) and (12, 97). What is its slope?::6|7|-6|5": "Slope is the change in y over the change in x: 97 minus 19, over 12 minus negative 1, which is 78 over 13, giving 6.",
    "A line with a slope of -5 passes through the point (4, -24). What is the line's y-intercept?::-5|4|-4|-3": "Plug the point into y equals mx plus b: negative 24 equals negative 5 times 4, plus b. That's negative 5 times 4, which is negative 20, so b is negative 24 minus negative 20, or negative 4.",
    "A line with a slope of 4 passes through the point (6, 22). What is the line's y-intercept?::2|-1|-3|-2": "Plug the point into y equals mx plus b: 22 equals 4 times 6, plus b. That's 4 times 6, which is 24, so b is 22 minus 24, or negative 2.",
    "A savings account starts at 157 and grows by 22 each week. What is the balance after 12 weeks?::-421|421|422|420": "Start from the initial value, 157, and add the rate times the number of periods: 157 plus 22 times 12, which is 157 plus 264, giving 421.",
    "A theater's ticket sales total starts at 148 and grows by 22 each week. What is the ticket total after 14 weeks?::456|455|-456|457": "Start from the initial value, 148, and add the rate times the number of periods: 148 plus 22 times 14, which is 148 plus 308, giving 456.",
    "The function g is defined by g(x) = 2x + 9. For what value of x does g(x) = 21?::6|7|5|-6": "Set the function equal to 21 and solve: 21 equals 2x, plus 9. Subtract 9 from both sides: 2x equals 12. Divide by 2, and x is 6.",
    "The function g is defined by g(x) = -5x + 17. For what value of x does g(x) = -3?::-4|3|4|5": "Set the function equal to negative 3 and solve: negative 3 equals negative 5x, plus 17. Subtract 17 from both sides: negative 5x equals negative 20. Divide by negative 5, and x is 4.",
    "A linear function has the following values: f(1) = 11, f(2) = 17, f(3) = 23, f(4) = 29. What is the rate of change of this function?::7|5|-6|6": "Look at how the output changes between consecutive rows of the table — since the input always increases by 1 each time, that difference directly gives the rate of change: 6.",
    "A linear function has the following values: f(2) = 38, f(3) = 32, f(4) = 26, f(5) = 20. What is the rate of change of this function?::-5|-7|6|-6": "Look at how the output changes between consecutive rows of the table — since the input always increases by 1 each time, that difference directly gives the rate of change: negative 6.",
    "If f(x) = 9x + 4, what is f(1)?::12|-13|13|14": "Plug 1 in for x: 9 times 1, plus 4, which is 9, plus 4, giving 13.",
    "If f(x) = -8x + 37, what is f(15)?::83|-84|-83|-82": "Plug 15 in for x: negative 8 times 15, plus 37, which is negative 120, plus 37, giving negative 83.",
    "A line passes through (2, -6) and (6, 18). What is its slope?::-6|6|7|5": "Slope is the change in y over the change in x: 18 minus negative 6, over 6 minus 2, which is 24 over 4, giving 6.",
    "A line passes through (-3, -11) and (-17, 45). What is its slope?::-4|4|-5|-3": "Slope is the change in y over the change in x: 45 minus negative 11, over negative 17 minus negative 3, which is 56 over negative 14, giving negative 4.",
    "A line with a slope of -1 passes through the point (9, 0). What is the line's y-intercept?::9|10|8|-9": "Plug the point into y equals negative x plus b: 0 equals negative 9, plus b. That's negative 9, so b is 0 minus negative 9, or 9.",
    "A line with a slope of 9 passes through the point (4, -22). What is the line's y-intercept?::-59|-58|58|-57": "Plug the point into y equals mx plus b: negative 22 equals 9 times 4, plus b. That's 9 times 4, which is 36, so b is negative 22 minus 36, or negative 58.",
    "A plant's height starts at 30 and grows by 25 each week. What is the height after 12 weeks?::331|329|-330|330": "Start from the initial value, 30, and add the rate times the number of periods: 30 plus 25 times 12, which is 30 plus 300, giving 330.",
    "A bakery's daily loaf output starts at 158 and grows by 14 each day. What is the loaf output after 15 days?::368|369|367|-368": "Start from the initial value, 158, and add the rate times the number of periods: 158 plus 14 times 15, which is 158 plus 210, giving 368.",
    "The function g is defined by g(x) = 2x - 8. For what value of x does g(x) = -14?::-4|3|-3|-2": "Set the function equal to negative 14 and solve: negative 14 equals 2x, minus 8. Add 8 to both sides: 2x equals negative 6. Divide by 2, and x is negative 3.",
    "The function g is defined by g(x) = 9x + 6. For what value of x does g(x) = 33?::4|3|2|-3": "Set the function equal to 33 and solve: 33 equals 9x, plus 6. Subtract 6 from both sides: 9x equals 27. Divide by 9, and x is 3.",
    "A linear function has the following values: f(0) = -2, f(1) = -7, f(2) = -12, f(3) = -17. What is the rate of change of this function?::5|-5|-4|-6": "Look at how the output changes between consecutive rows of the table — since the input always increases by 1 each time, that difference directly gives the rate of change: negative 5.",
    "A linear function has the following values: f(4) = 16, f(5) = 3, f(6) = -10, f(7) = -23. What is the rate of change of this function?::-12|-14|-13|13": "Look at how the output changes between consecutive rows of the table — since the input always increases by 1 each time, that difference directly gives the rate of change: negative 13.",
    "If f(x) = 8x - 13, what is f(10)?::67|68|66|-67": "Plug 10 in for x: 8 times 10, minus 13, which is 80, minus 13, giving 67.",
    "If f(x) = 6x - 5, what is f(-15)?::-94|95|-95|-96": "Plug negative 15 in for x: 6 times negative 15, minus 5, which is negative 90, minus 5, giving negative 95.",
    "A line passes through (-6, 3) and (-8, 5). What is its slope?::0|-2|1|-1": "Slope is the change in y over the change in x: 5 minus 3, over negative 8 minus negative 6, which is 2 over negative 2, giving negative 1.",
    "A line passes through (-12, -12) and (0, -84). What is its slope?::6|-7|-5|-6": "Slope is the change in y over the change in x: negative 84 minus negative 12, over 0 minus negative 12, which is negative 72 over 12, giving negative 6.",
    "A line with a slope of 8 passes through the point (-2, -23). What is the line's y-intercept?::-8|7|-7|-6": "Plug the point into y equals mx plus b: negative 23 equals 8 times negative 2, plus b. That's 8 times negative 2, which is negative 16, so b is negative 23 minus negative 16, or negative 7.",
    "A line with a slope of -8 passes through the point (-9, 52). What is the line's y-intercept?::-19|-21|20|-20": "Plug the point into y equals mx plus b: 52 equals negative 8 times negative 9, plus b. That's negative 8 times negative 9, which is 72, so b is 52 minus 72, or negative 20.",
    "A company's inventory starts at 93 and grows by 17 each day. What is the stock after 6 days?::-195|195|196|194": "Start from the initial value, 93, and add the rate times the number of periods: 93 plus 17 times 6, which is 93 plus 102, giving 195.",
    "A factory's production count starts at 147 and grows by 13 each week. What is the output after 12 weeks?::302|-303|304|303": "Start from the initial value, 147, and add the rate times the number of periods: 147 plus 13 times 12, which is 147 plus 156, giving 303.",
