    "A linear function has the following values: f(-3) = 17, f(-2) = 12, f(-1) = 7, f(0) = 2. What is the rate of change of this function?::5|-5|-4|-6": "Look at how the output changes between consecutive rows of the table — since the input always increases by 1 each time, that difference directly gives the rate of change: negative 5.",
