    "A linear function has the following values: f(1) = 9, f(2) = 15, f(3) = 21, f(4) = 27. What is the rate of change of this function?": "Look at how the output changes between consecutive rows of the table — since the input always increases by 1 each time, that difference directly gives the rate of change: 6.",
