    "A linear function has the following values: f(-3) = -9, f(-2) = -5, f(-1) = -1, f(0) = 3. What is the rate of change of this function?": "Look at how the output changes between consecutive rows of the table — since the input always increases by 1 each time, that difference directly gives the rate of change: 4.",
    "A linear function has the following values: f(7) = 37, f(8) = 46, f(9) = 55, f(10) = 64. What is the rate of change of this function?": "Look at how the output changes between consecutive rows of the table — since the input always increases by 1 each time, that difference directly gives the rate of change: 9.",
