    "A line has a slope of -1/5. What is the slope of a line perpendicular to it?::-5|-1/5|5|1/5": "A perpendicular slope is always the negative reciprocal of the original — flip it and switch its sign. The negative reciprocal of negative 1 over 5 is 5.",
