    "What is the y-intercept of the line -x + 4y = 36?::(9, 0)|(0, -9)|(0, 11)|(0, 9)": "Set x to 0 and simplify: that leaves 4y equal to 36, so y is 9. The y-intercept is the point (0, 9).",
    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (0, 1) and (-6, 25)?::(-2, 8)|(-1, 9)|(-2, 9)|(-2, 10)": "First find the slope between the two points: 25 minus 1, over negative 6 minus 0, which is negative 4. Starting from (0, 1) and moving to x equals negative 2, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: negative 4 times (negative 2 minus 0), which is 8. That gives y equals 9, so the point (negative 2, 9) lies on the line.",
    "A line has a slope of -7/2. What is the slope of a line perpendicular to it?::-2/7|7/2|2/7|-7/2": "A perpendicular slope is always the negative reciprocal of the original — flip it and switch its sign. The negative reciprocal of negative 7 over 2 is 2 over 7.",
    "A line passes through the point (2, 11) and has a slope of 8. What is the equation of the line in slope-intercept form?::y = 8x - 3|y = 8x - 5|y = 8x + 5|y = -8x - 5": "Start from point-slope form: y minus 11, equals 8 times (x minus 2). Distribute: y equals 8x, minus 16, plus 11. Combine the constant terms: y equals 8x, minus 5.",
    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (4, -10) and (1, 5)?::(0, 9)|(1, 10)|(0, 12)|(0, 10)": "First find the slope between the two points: 5 minus negative 10, over 1 minus 4, which is negative 5. Starting from (4, negative 10) and moving to x equals 0, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: negative 5 times (0 minus 4), which is 20. That gives y equals 10, so the point (0, 10) lies on the line.",
    "What is the x-intercept of the line y = -5x - 25?::(-5, 0)|(5, 0)|(0, -25)|(-3, 0)": "Set y to 0: 0 equals negative 5x, minus 25. Move the 25 to the other side: negative 5x equals 25. Divide by negative 5, and x is negative 5.",
    "A line passes through the point (8, -6) and has a slope of 1. What is the equation of the line in slope-intercept form?::y = x + 14|y = -x - 14|y = x - 16|y = x - 14": "Start from point-slope form: y minus negative 6, equals 1 times (x minus 8). Distribute: y equals x, minus 8, minus 6. Combine the constant terms: y equals x, minus 14.",
    "What is the slope of the line -12x + 3y = 6?::5|3|-4|4": "Solve for y: 3y equals 6, plus 12x. Divide every term by 3: y equals 4x, plus 2 — so the slope, the coefficient of x, is 4.",
    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (0, -2) and (8, -30)?::(0, -4)|(0, -3)|(1, -2)|(0, -2)": "First find the slope between the two points: negative 30 minus negative 2, over 8 minus 0, which is negative 7 over 2. Starting from (0, negative 2) and moving to x equals 0, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: negative 7 over 2 times (0 minus 0), which is 0. That gives y equals negative 2, so the point (0, negative 2) lies on the line.",
    "A line has a slope of 1/3. What is the slope of a line perpendicular to it?::3|-2|-3|1/3": "A perpendicular slope is always the negative reciprocal of the original — flip it and switch its sign. The negative reciprocal of 1 over 3 is negative 3.",
    "What is the y-intercept of the line -6x - 3y = 24?::(0, 8)|(0, -10)|(-8, 0)|(0, -8)": "Set x to 0 and simplify: that leaves negative 3y equal to 24, so y is negative 8. The y-intercept is the point (0, negative 8).",
    "What is the y-intercept of the line -6x - y = 7?::(0, -5)|(0, -7)|(0, 7)|(-7, 0)": "Set x to 0 and simplify: that leaves negative y equal to 7, so y is negative 7. The y-intercept is the point (0, negative 7).",
    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (6, 2) and (18, -6)?::(0, 5)|(0, 6)|(1, 6)|(0, 8)": "First find the slope between the two points: negative 6 minus 2, over 18 minus 6, which is negative 2 over 3. Starting from (6, 2) and moving to x equals 0, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: negative 2 over 3 times (0 minus 6), which is 4. That gives y equals 6, so the point (0, 6) lies on the line.",
    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (-4, 0) and (-2, 2)?::(0, 4)|(0, 5)|(0, 3)|(1, 4)": "First find the slope between the two points: 2 minus 0, over negative 2 minus negative 4, which is 1. Starting from (negative 4, 0) and moving to x equals 0, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: 1 times (0 minus negative 4), which is 4. That gives y equals 4, so the point (0, 4) lies on the line.",
    "What is the y-intercept of the line -5x - y = 10?::(0, -12)|(-10, 0)|(0, 10)|(0, -10)": "Set x to 0 and simplify: that leaves negative y equal to 10, so y is negative 10. The y-intercept is the point (0, negative 10).",
    "A line passes through the point (-2, 11) and has a slope of 8. What is the equation of the line in slope-intercept form?::y = 8x - 27|y = -8x + 27|y = 8x + 29|y = 8x + 27": "Start from point-slope form: y minus 11, equals 8 times (x minus negative 2). Distribute: y equals 8x, plus 16, plus 11. Combine the constant terms: y equals 8x, plus 27.",
    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (4, -14) and (2, -26)?::(0, -40)|(0, -39)|(1, -38)|(0, -38)": "First find the slope between the two points: negative 26 minus negative 14, over 2 minus 4, which is 6. Starting from (4, negative 14) and moving to x equals 0, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: 6 times (0 minus 4), which is negative 24. That gives y equals negative 38, so the point (0, negative 38) lies on the line.",
    "What is the x-intercept of the line y = -5x - 50?::(0, -50)|(-8, 0)|(-10, 0)|(10, 0)": "Set y to 0: 0 equals negative 5x, minus 50. Move the 50 to the other side: negative 5x equals 50. Divide by negative 5, and x is negative 10.",
    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (8, -12) and (9, -7)?::(0, -52)|(0, -54)|(1, -52)|(0, -53)": "First find the slope between the two points: negative 7 minus negative 12, over 9 minus 8, which is 5. Starting from (8, negative 12) and moving to x equals 0, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: 5 times (0 minus 8), which is negative 40. That gives y equals negative 52, so the point (0, negative 52) lies on the line.",
    "What is the slope of the line -3x + y = 1?::-3|3|4|2": "Solve for y: y equals 1, plus 3x. y equals 3x, plus 1 — so the slope, the coefficient of x, is 3.",
    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (-6, 4) and (-18, 0)?::(0, 8)|(0, 6)|(1, 6)|(0, 5)": "First find the slope between the two points: 0 minus 4, over negative 18 minus negative 6, which is 1 over 3. Starting from (negative 6, 4) and moving to x equals 0, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: 1 over 3 times (0 minus negative 6), which is 2. That gives y equals 6, so the point (0, 6) lies on the line.",
    "A line has a slope of -1/4. What is the slope of a line perpendicular to it?::4|-1/4|-4|2": "A perpendicular slope is always the negative reciprocal of the original — flip it and switch its sign. The negative reciprocal of negative 1 over 4 is 4.",
    "A line has a slope of 9/2. What is the slope of a line perpendicular to it?::-9/2|9/2|2/9|-2/9": "A perpendicular slope is always the negative reciprocal of the original — flip it and switch its sign. The negative reciprocal of 9 over 2 is negative 2 over 9.",
    "What is the y-intercept of the line -6x + 2y = 4?::(0, -2)|(2, 0)|(0, 4)|(0, 2)": "Set x to 0 and simplify: that leaves 2y equal to 4, so y is 2. The y-intercept is the point (0, 2).",
