    "Which point lies on the line that passes through (-5, -5) and (2, -19)?::(-2, -12)|(-1, -11)|(-2, -11)|(-2, -10)": "First find the slope between the two points: negative 19 minus negative 5, over 2 minus negative 5, which is negative 2. Starting from (negative 5, negative 5) and moving to x equals negative 2, the y-value changes by the slope times the change in x: negative 2 times (negative 2 minus negative 5), which is negative 6. That gives y equals negative 11, so the point (negative 2, negative 11) lies on the line.",
    "A line passes through the point (-12, -3) and has a slope of 1. What is the equation of the line in slope-intercept form?::y = x + 9|y = -x + 9|y = x - 9|y = x + 11": "Start from point-slope form: y minus negative 3, equals 1 times (x minus negative 12). Distribute: y equals x, plus 12, minus 3. Combine the constant terms: y equals x, plus 9.",
    "A line passes through the point (2, 13) and has a slope of 8. What is the equation of the line in slope-intercept form?::y = 8x - 1|y = 8x - 3|y = 8x + 3|y = -8x - 3": "Start from point-slope form: y minus 13, equals 8 times (x minus 2). Distribute: y equals 8x, minus 16, plus 13. Combine the constant terms: y equals 8x, minus 3.",
